AaveV3Adapter_withdraw
  ├── when the caller is not the vault
  │   └── it should revert
  ├── when the amount is type(uint256).max
  │   ├── when only buffered assets exist
  │   │   └── it should transfer the buffer without calling Aave
  │   ├── when buffered and protocol assets exist
  │   │   └── it should withdraw both and clear the buffer
  │   ├── when the actual withdrawn amount is less than the TVL
  │   │   └── it should revert
  │   ├── when the withdrawn shortfall exceeds the rounding tolerance
  │   │   └── it should revert
  │   ├── when the withdrawn shortfall is within the rounding tolerance
  │   │   └── it should succeed
  │   ├── when the withdrawn amount is zero
  │   │   └── it should revert
  │   └── when the actual withdrawn amount is gte the TVL
  │       ├── it should emit a Withdraw event
  │       └── it should transfer USDC to the vault
  └── when performing an epoch withdraw
      ├── when the request is less than the buffer
      │   └── it should transfer the request and retain the unused buffer
      ├── when the request equals the buffer
      │   └── it should transfer the buffer without calling Aave
      ├── when the request exceeds the buffer
      │   ├── it should consume the buffer before withdrawing from Aave
      │   ├── it should validate the protocol leg independently
      │   └── it should restore the buffer if the protocol leg reverts
      ├── when the amount exceeds the TVL
      │   └── it should revert
      ├── when the actual withdrawn amount is less than the requested amount
      │   └── it should revert
      ├── when the withdrawn shortfall exceeds the rounding tolerance
      │   └── it should revert
      ├── when the withdrawn shortfall equals the rounding tolerance
      │   └── it should succeed
      ├── when the withdrawn amount is zero
      │   └── it should revert
      └── when the actual withdrawn amount is gte the requested amount
          ├── it should emit a Withdraw event
          └── it should transfer USDC to the vault
